// omarchy-kids-trimmed.jsonc — root-owned omarchy-menu extension for
// Levels 1 and 2 (SPEC.md R-DESK-4, Q23).
//
// UNVERIFIED SCHEMA. omarchy-menu's extension/plugin format was not
// available in the reference material this repo was written against
// (only two of Omarchy's default.hypr.bindings.* files were available,
// no omarchy-menu source or docs), so the shape below -- a "hide" list
// of entry ids -- is a guess at the simplest schema that could satisfy
// R-DESK-4's wording ("through a root-owned menu extension"), not a
// confirmed one. Confirm the real extension format on a running Omarchy
// 4.0.2 box before wiring this in anywhere, and correct the entry ids
// (install/update/setup below are also guesses at what omarchy-menu
// calls those rows).
//
// This is also, deliberately, not the only thing enforcing R-DESK-4:
// Level 1 has no bar/shell at all (share/hyprland/L1.lua's exec-once
// starts only the big-tile launcher, never omarchy-launch-shell), so
// there is nothing to trim there. Level 2 runs the Kids Mode launcher,
// not Omarchy's own shell, and share/hyprland/L2.lua rebinds
// Super+Space to that launcher instead of "omarchy-menu toggle"
// (Appendix E). So even if this file's hiding mechanism turns out not
// to be supported at all, no Level 1 or 2 keybinding reaches the
// untrimmed menu. What this file's hiding (if supported) would
// additionally cover is mouse/bar access to the menu, which is why
// it's still worth getting right rather than dropping.
{
  "hide": ["install", "update", "setup"]
}
